@startuml FintechPerformanceArchitecture

title Frontend Performance & Data Strategy

rectangle "React UI Layer" {
    component "Pages"
    component "Components"
}

rectangle "State Layer" {
    component "DataContext\n(Cache + State Store)" as Data
    component "AuthContext"
    component "SettingsContext"
}

rectangle "Access Layer" {
    component "Domain Hooks\n(thin wrappers)" as Hooks
}

rectangle "Service Layer (FE)" {
    component "Services\n(accounts, tx, analytics)"
    component "Request Manager\n(dedup + batching)" as ReqMgr
}

rectangle "HTTP Layer" {
    component "API Client (Axios)" as API
}

rectangle "Backend" {
    component "FastAPI"
}

' Flow
Components --> Hooks
Hooks --> Data

' Cache-first strategy
Data --> Data : In-memory cache (TTL)
Hooks --> Data : read-first

' Miss → fetch
Data --> Services
Services --> ReqMgr
ReqMgr --> API
API --> FastAPI

' Deduplication
ReqMgr --> ReqMgr : prevent duplicate inflight calls

' Batching (example for analytics)
ReqMgr --> API : batch GET /analytics/*

' Re-render control
Data --> Components : selective subscriptions\n(useMemo/useCallback)

note right of Data
Strategies:
- Cache with TTL (e.g., 30–120s)
- Stale-while-revalidate
- Normalized state (by id)
- Pagination for large lists
end note

note bottom of ReqMgr
Optimizations:
- Request deduplication
- Batch endpoints where possible
- Retry with backoff
end note

@enduml